
[pr-check]
ok - raw-byte parser accepts canonical URLs and rejects the complete adversarial matrix
ok - plain-http Forgejo poll resolves only the exact host-and-port login
ok - Forgejo login match parses tea's JSON in every line shape, in the helper and the static poll
ok - the scan records the PR a done line reports and leaves prose, scouts and recorded PRs alone

[pr-merge]
ok - fm-pr-merge merges a Forgejo pull request through tea api instead of refusing it
ok - fm-pr-merge resolves the exact host-and-port login and refuses another port's login
ok - fm-pr-merge refuses when zero or more than one tea login matches the pull request's host

[rex]
ok - rex: the marks producer plans from status, writes once, repairs without re-notifying, clears on resolve, and honors off

[osc]
ok - status transitions: blocked->done, final record survives parent death

[inactive]
ok - secondmate preserves an unrecorded plain-http Forgejo PR from its ledger line

[fleet]
ok - snapshot projects plain-http Forgejo PRs from status and backlog records

[backlog]
ok - session start replays a recorded plain-http Forgejo close with its URL as a note
ok - session start replays a recorded https Forgejo close with its --pr link
ok - recovery rejects malformed PR URL values

[board]
ok - build accepts plain-http Forgejo PR URLs on cards and landed rows

[teardown]
ok - a ledger row carrying a plain-http PR URL still proves the anchored continuation
